_:r51b109b54e0cfc7d58191ce9_n9749884d7446473b865535d83bb61528b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://dandiarchive.org\">Distributed Archives for Neurophysiology Data Integration (DANDI)</a> is a platform for publishing, sharing, and processing neurophysiology data funded by the <a href=\"https://braininitiative.nih.gov/\">BRAIN Initiative</a>. The platform is now available for data upload and distribution, and provides supplementary client tools to assist with introspection and organization of data following <a href=\"#nwb\">NWB standard</a>. </p> <ul> <li> <a href=\"https://reporter.nih.gov/project-details/9795271\">NIH (#1R24MH117295-01A1)</a>. PIs: <a href=\"https://mcgovern.mit.edu/profile/satrajit-ghosh/\" class=\"centroid\">S. Ghosh</a> and <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"https://github.com/dandi/dandisets\">dandisets</a>: a <a href=\"#datalad\">DataLad</a> superdataset providing unified access to all public DANDI datasets, with individual dandisets also mirrored as DataLad datasets in the <a href=\"https://github.com/dandisets\">dandisets</a> GitHub organization and their Zarr stores in <a href=\"https://github.com/dandizarrs\">dandizarrs</a>. </li> <li> <a href=\"https://github.com/dandi-compute\">DANDI Compute</a>: an experimental reproducible-computing initiative running processing pipelines directly on DANDI assets. The first campaign applies the <a href=\"https://github.com/AllenNeuralDynamics/aind-ephys-pipeline\">AIND ephys pipeline</a> to electrophysiology dandisets, with orchestration code and a public job queue hosted in the <a href=\"https://github.com/dandi-compute\">dandi-compute</a> GitHub organization. </li> </ul>" .
_:r51b109b54e0cfc7d58191ce9_n9749884d7446473b865535d83bb61528b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
